; Stage 15 B2a (design/stage15-stress-test/name-resolution.md §8.3 R3, §11.4 R7)
; — the reported defect, pinned as an error.
;
; This file imports lib/nsdescribe.nuc with `(import-prefixed … dpx)`, so the
; ONE qualifier it bound for that library is `dpx`. The library's own namespace
; is `dp`, and before B2a `dp/Describe` resolved anyway — `protocol-lookup`
; probed the raw spelling against a registry keyed by defining namespace, with
; nothing consulting the import environment at all. That made an import prefix
; an *addition* to the spellings in scope rather than the definition of them,
; which is §3 defect #3.
;
; The positive half — the same protocol reached as `dpx/Describe`, boxed, and
; dispatched — is examples/w9-dyn-ns.nuc, which asserts results rather than an
; exit code. Here the assertion is that the diagnostic is a SCOPE diagnostic: it
; names the qualifier, says what a prefixed import binds, and lists what this
; file can actually spell. Degrading to "not defined anywhere in this compilation
; unit" would be false — the protocol is defined, the import graph reaches it,
; and one edit to the reference fixes it.
(import-use "stdio.h")
(import-prefixed nsdescribe dpx)

(defstruct Cat n:i32)
(defn describe ((self (ref Cat))):i32 (return (+ 100 (self n))))

(extend Cat dp/Describe)

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
